{"name":"Swagger","hex":"#19b6b5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"swagger","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To behave (especially to walk or carry oneself) in a pompous, superior manner.","To boast or brag noisily; to bluster; to bully."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Confidence, pride.","A bold or arrogant strut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swagger"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swagger (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Swagger is a suite of tools for API developers from SmartBear Software and a former specification upon which the OpenAPI Specification is based."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swagger_(software)","wikidata":"Q39069667"},{"title":"Swagger (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Swagger is an American sports drama television series created by Reggie Rock Bythewood. Loosely inspired by the experiences of NBA player Kevin Durant, the series premiered on October 29, 2021 on Apple TV+. In June 2022, the series was renewed for a second season. In November 2023, the series was canceled after two seasons. Swagger has garnered critical acclaim from critics for its writing, acting, production values and social commentary."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/Swagger_TV_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swagger_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q60760778"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/Swagger_TV_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/Swagger_TV_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwagger_TV_poster.jpg"}],"sounds":{"swagger":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/En-au-swagger.ogg?utm_source=en